      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 12. Agency heads should take steps to insure that compensatory time earned be used as quickly as possible thereafter to the extent that the needs of the agency will permit. It shall be the responsibility of the employee to request permission to use such overtime. Compensatory time not used by the employee may be carried over from year to year only to the extent that the needs of the agency have not permitted the employee to use such time. Requests for carry-over and approval must be in writing. Approval must come from the agency head. All of the above actions must comply with the Fair Labor Standards Act where applicable.",
